{
 "_comment": "Per-SKU order limits in two tiers, plus the retired list. `limits` is the EXTERNAL tier and the default on purpose: if the staff override never runs, everyone gets the tighter partner number, which fails safe. `internal` is applied on top for Millboard staff by the mb_sof_sku_limits filter in the wc-account-sample-ordering component. `retired` lines are dropped from the tool entirely by that component's mb_sof_in_scope filter.",
 "_external_source": "Millboard_sample_ordering_audit_DH_updated.xlsx column I, signed off by Dan Hernandez. His scope: external requests from distributors and customers through the partner portal only. Unchanged from his 30 Sep sheet.",
 "_internal_source": "Dan Hernandez, 1 Oct 2026: 'I would just set their order allowance 3x the amount we allow for distributors as a general rule of thumb.' So this is external x 3, derived not hand-entered. Re-derive it if the external numbers change.",
 "_retired_source": "Column K, Dan Hernandez 1 Oct 2026. 23 marketing/POS lines and 1 presenter pack: 'I have retired some POS due to not knowing our position on the stands for next year.' Display racks and sample panels, so this is expected to be revisited.",
